			<div class="content" id="post-content-2447673">
									

<p>I did consider making all information of SCP-2359 hazardous, but the removal of the indistinct line between safe and hazardous knowledge - and the possibility that the foundation is wrong in what it believes to be safe - made my own article seem bland to me. Also, it would remove impact of the twist, which implies that the article has been doctored by SCP-2359 to make it hazardous. If it was always hazardous, that twist would be rendered ineffectual.</p>
<p>My only regret in changing from &quot;memetic&quot; to &quot;cognitohazardous&quot; is that the later is a veritable eyesore on the page. At the very least, it doesn't flow anywhere near as well. That's a trifling issue, though, so it doesn't merit concern.</p>
<p>Anyway, the changes have been made now, along with some formatting changes to place the two interviews into collapsibles. Nice to have the article up to snuff.</p>

